# The app captures the site renders. Same reasoning as apps/apple/.gitattributes:
# large binaries rewritten in full whenever the UI changes, so without LFS every
# screenshot refresh adds the whole set to history, forever, in every clone.
#
# They are committed rather than generated at build time because `astro build`
# imports them through astro:assets — a clone that has not just run
# `make screenshots` still has to build the site, CI included. Without `lfs: true`
# on the checkout these arrive as 131-byte pointer files still named .png, and
# sharp then fails with an error about the image format rather than about the
# checkout.
#
# This file lives in apps/website/ rather than at the repo root because its
# patterns are relative to its own directory. Hoisting it up would silently stop
# matching, and the next refresh would commit these as ordinary blobs.
src/assets/shots/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The tour loop `make site-video` writes, for the same reason: re-rendered in
# full after every capture run. Served from public/ rather than imported, so a
# pointer file here would not fail the build; it would deploy as a 130-byte
# "video". Both website jobs in ci.yml check out with `lfs: true`.
public/video/*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
